            ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${ao})`; 
            if(isV) ctx.fillRect(-dh/2, -dw/2, dh, dw); else ctx.fillRect(dx, dy, dw, dh); 
        }
        ctx.restore();
    };

    /**
     * MULTI-PASS COMPOSITE RENDERER
     */

    // PASS 1: THE SOLID BED (Ground Warp foundation)
    for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
        const waYId = warpYarnSequence[c % warpYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
        const waDef = warpYarns[waYId];
        const waTex = textureMap.get(`warp-${waYId}`);
        if (!waTex || !waDef) continue;
        const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;
        for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
            const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];
            if (gY > CANVAS_HEIGHT || gY + gH < 0) continue;
            drawThread(waTex, gX, gY, gW, gH, waDef.thickness || 1, waDef.spacing || 0, true, 1.0, 0, 0, 0);
        }
    }

    // PASS 2: WEFT INTEGRATION (Interlaced Weft)
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        const wYId = weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
        const wDef = weftYarns[wYId];
        const wTex = textureMap.get(`weft-${wYId}`);
        if (!wDef || !wTex) continue;

        const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];
        if (gY > CANVAS_HEIGHT || gY + gH < 0) continue;

        for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const wTopR = structure[pR]?.[pC] || false;
            const isOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !wTopR : wTopR;
            const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;

            let op = 1.0;
            let ao = 0, taper = 0;

            if (!isOver) {
                // Weft is under. Render with lower opacity to blend with "bed" warp
                op = wDef.isExtraWeft ? (hideFloats ? 0 : (wDef.extraFloatOpacity ?? 0.08)) : 0.6;
            } else {
                // Weft is over. Check neighbors for AO
                const prevW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[pR]?.[(pC-1+cols)%cols] || false) : !(structure[pR]?.[(pC-1+cols)%cols] || false);
                const nextW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[pR]?.[(pC+1)%cols] || false) : !(structure[pR]?.[(pC+1)%cols] || false);
                if (prevW || nextW) { 
                    ao = (wDef.bindingDepth || 0.1) * 1.5; 
                    taper = (wDef.floatTaper || 0) * 0.5;
                }
            }
            drawThread(wTex, gX, gY, gW, gH, wDef.thickness || 1, wDef.spacing || 0, false, op, isOver ? (wDef.extraOverlap ?? 0) : 0, ao, taper);
        }
    }

    // PASS 3: OCCLUSION SHADOWS
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];
        if (gY > CANVAS_HEIGHT || gY + gH < 0) continue;

        for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const wTopR = structure[pR]?.[pC] || false;
            const weftIsOnTop = viewSide === 'face' ? !wTopR : wTopR;
            const def = weftIsOnTop ? weftYarns[weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length]] : warpYarns[warpYarnSequence[pC % warpYarnSequence.length]];
            const sTh = (def?.shadowThrow ?? 1.5) * SS_FACTOR;
            const sAn = (def?.shadowAngle ?? 135) * Math.PI/180;

            if (sTh > 0 && def) {
                const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;
                ctx.globalAlpha = 0.3;
                ctx.drawImage(shadowCanvas, (gX + gW/2) + Math.cos(sAn)*sTh - gW*2, (gY + gH/2) + Math.sin(sAn)*sTh - gH*2, gW*4, gH*4);
            }
        }
    }

    // PASS 4: SURFACE INTERLACE (Foreground Warp)
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];
        if (gY > CANVAS_HEIGHT || gY + gH < 0) continue;

        for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const wTopR = structure[pR]?.[pC] || false;
            const warpIsOnTop = viewSide === 'face' ? wTopR : !wTopR;

            if (warpIsOnTop) {
                const waYId = warpYarnSequence[pC % warpYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
                const waDef = warpYarns[waYId];
                const waTex = textureMap.get(`warp-${waYId}`);
                if (waTex && waDef) {
                    const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;
                    let waAO = 0, waT = 0;
                    const upW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[(pR-1+rows)%rows]?.[pC] || false) : !(structure[(pR-1+rows)%rows]?.[pC] || false);
                    const dnW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[(pR+1)%rows]?.[pC] || false) : !(structure[(pR+1)%rows]?.[pC] || false);
                    if (!upW || !dnW) { 
                        waAO = (waDef.bindingDepth || 0.1) * 1.5; 
                        waT = (waDef.floatTaper || 0) * 0.5; 
                    }
                    drawThread(waTex, gX, gY, gW, gH, waDef.thickness || 1, waDef.spacing || 0, true, 1.0, 0, waAO, waT);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return canvas;
};

import { YarnDefinition, DensityZone } from '../types';
import { generateYarnTexture } from './yarnRenderer';

interface RenderOptions {
    weavePattern: string[][];
    structure: boolean[][];
    epi: number;
    ppi: number;
    dentingPlan?: number[];
    weftZones?: DensityZone[];
    warpYarns: { [key: string]: YarnDefinition };
    weftYarns: { [key: string]: YarnDefinition };
    warpYarnSequence: string[];
    weftYarnSequence: string[];
    viewSide: 'face' | 'back';
    dpi: number;
    width: number; 
    height: number; 
    hideFloats?: boolean; 
    backgroundColor?: string; 
    smoothingQuality?: 'low' | 'medium' | 'high' | 'none';
}

/**
 * FABRIC RENDERER V15.0 - PRO INDUSTRIAL GRADE
 * Uses Continuous Layer Buffering to eliminate "Black Bleed" and grid artifacts.
 */
export const renderFabricToCanvas = (options: RenderOptions): HTMLCanvasElement => {
    const { 
        weavePattern = [], structure = [], epi, ppi, dentingPlan,
        warpYarns = {}, weftYarns = {}, warpYarnSequence = [], weftYarnSequence = [],
        viewSide, dpi, width: displayW, height: displayH,
        hideFloats = false,
        backgroundColor = '#121215', // Dark neutral substrate
        smoothingQuality = 'high'
    } = options;

    const rows = weavePattern.length;
    const cols = weavePattern[0] ? weavePattern[0].length : 0;
    if (rows === 0 || cols === 0) return document.createElement('canvas');

    // --- SCALING & RESOLUTION ---
    const SS_FACTOR = 1.5; // High-fidelity supersampling
    const PX_PER_INCH = dpi * SS_FACTOR;
    const CANVAS_WIDTH = Math.round((displayW / 96) * PX_PER_INCH);
    const CANVAS_HEIGHT = Math.round((displayH / 96) * PX_PER_INCH);

    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = Math.max(1, CANVAS_WIDTH);
    canvas.height = Math.max(1, CANVAS_HEIGHT);
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false });
    if (!ctx) return canvas;

    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = smoothingQuality !== 'none';
    ctx.imageSmoothingQuality = smoothingQuality === 'high' ? 'high' : 'medium';

    // 1. Pre-fill with a "Substrate" color (Dark variant of average yarn color)
    ctx.fillStyle = backgroundColor;
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

    // --- GEOMETRY: WARP ---
    const safePlan = (dentingPlan && dentingPlan.length > 0) ? dentingPlan : [1];
    const avgThreadsPerDent = Math.max(1, safePlan.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / safePlan.length);
    const dentWidthPx = (PX_PER_INCH * avgThreadsPerDent) / Math.max(1, epi);

    const warpPositions: {x: number, w: number}[] = [];
    let currentX = 0;
    let dIdx = 0;
    while (currentX < CANVAS_WIDTH + 100) {
        const threads = safePlan[dIdx % safePlan.length];
        const w = threads === 0 ? dentWidthPx : dentWidthPx / threads;
        const count = threads === 0 ? 1 : threads;
        for (let k = 0; k < count; k++) {
            warpPositions.push({ x: currentX, w });
            currentX += w;
        }
        dIdx++;
    }
    const totalCols = warpPositions.length;

    // --- GEOMETRY: WEFT ---
    const rowY: number[] = [];
    const rowHeights: number[] = [];
    const nominalH = PX_PER_INCH / Math.max(1, ppi);
    let currentY = 0;
    for (let r = 0; r < rows * 10; r++) { // Safety buffer for tiling
        const yid = weftYarnSequence.length > 0 ? weftYarnSequence[r % weftYarnSequence.length] : 'A';
        const preferred = weftYarns[yid]?.preferredPPI;
        let h = preferred ? (PX_PER_INCH / Math.max(1, preferred)) : nominalH;
        rowY.push(currentY);
        rowHeights.push(h);
        currentY += h; 
        if (currentY > CANVAS_HEIGHT + 100) break;
    }

    // --- TEXTURES ---
    const textureMap = new Map<string, HTMLCanvasElement>();
    const getTex = (id: string, type: 'warp' | 'weft') => {
        const key = `${type}-${id}`;
        if (textureMap.has(key)) return textureMap.get(key);
        const def = (type === 'warp' ? warpYarns : weftYarns)[id];
        if (!def) return null;
        const tex = generateYarnTexture(def, dpi * SS_FACTOR);
        textureMap.set(key, tex);
        return tex;
    };

    /**
     * LAYER 1: CONTINUOUS WARP BUFFER
     * We render all warps as full vertical columns.
     */
    const warpCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    warpCanvas.width = canvas.width; warpCanvas.height = canvas.height;
    const wCtx = warpCanvas.getContext('2d')!;

    warpPositions.forEach((pos, i) => {
        const yid = warpYarnSequence[i % warpYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
        const def = warpYarns[yid];
        const tex = getTex(yid, 'warp');
        if (!tex || !def) return;

        const expansion = 1.3; // Coverage expansion
        const dw = pos.w * (def.thickness || 1) * expansion;
        const dx = pos.x + pos.w/2 - dw/2;
        const phase = Math.floor((Math.abs(Math.sin(i * 123.45)) * 1000) % tex.width);

        wCtx.save();
        wCtx.translate(dx + dw/2, canvas.height/2);
        wCtx.rotate(Math.PI / 2);
        // Using repeat pattern to draw full vertical length instantly
        const pat = wCtx.createPattern(tex, 'repeat');
        if (pat) {
            const matrix = new DOMMatrix();
            matrix.scaleSelf(1, dw / tex.height);
            matrix.translateSelf(phase, 0);
            pat.setTransform(matrix);
            wCtx.fillStyle = pat;
            wCtx.fillRect(-canvas.height/2, -dw/2, canvas.height, dw);
        }
        wCtx.restore();
    });

    /**
     * LAYER 2: CONTINUOUS WEFT BUFFER
     * We render all wefts as full horizontal rows.
     */
    const weftCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    weftCanvas.width = canvas.width; weftCanvas.height = canvas.height;
    const wfCtx = weftCanvas.getContext('2d')!;

    rowY.forEach((y, i) => {
        const yid = weftYarnSequence[i % weftYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
        const def = weftYarns[yid];
        const tex = getTex(yid, 'weft');
        if (!tex || !def) return;

        const expansion = 1.3;
        const dh = rowHeights[i] * (def.thickness || 1) * expansion;
        const dy = y + rowHeights[i]/2 - dh/2;
        const phase = Math.floor((Math.abs(Math.sin(i * 543.21)) * 1000) % tex.width);

        wfCtx.save();
        wfCtx.translate(canvas.width/2, dy + dh/2);
        const pat = wfCtx.createPattern(tex, 'repeat');
        if (pat) {
            const matrix = new DOMMatrix();
            matrix.scaleSelf(1, dh / tex.height);
            matrix.translateSelf(phase, 0);
            pat.setTransform(matrix);
            wfCtx.fillStyle = pat;
            wfCtx.fillRect(-canvas.width/2, -dh/2, canvas.width, dh);
        }
        wfCtx.restore();
    });

    /**
     * LAYER 3: COMPOSITING
     * We use a smart segment-by-segment compositor to place foreground items.
     */

    // Pass 1: Draw the entire Warp Canvas as the background layer
    ctx.drawImage(warpCanvas, 0, 0);

    // Pass 2: Draw the segments of weft that are "Over"
    // We use sub-pixel "feathering" to make them look naturally woven.
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];

        for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const wTopR = structure[pR]?.[pC] || false;
            const weftIsOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !wTopR : wTopR;

            if (weftIsOver) {
                const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;
                // Draw a clip from the pre-rendered weft canvas
                // We add a tiny 0.5px vertical bleed to the clip to ensure segments touch perfectly
                ctx.drawImage(weftCanvas, gX, gY - 0.5, gW, gH + 1.0, gX, gY - 0.5, gW, gH + 1.0);

                // Physical shadow for depth
                const yid = weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length];
                const def = weftYarns[yid];
                const depth = (def?.bindingDepth || 0.1) * 0.8;
                if (depth > 0) {
                    // Check if previous or next warp is also "Under" weft. If not, draw shadow edge.
                    const prevW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[pR]?.[(pC-1+cols)%cols] || false) : !(structure[pR]?.[(pC-1+cols)%cols] || false);
                    if (prevW) {
                        ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${depth})`;
                        ctx.fillRect(gX, gY, gW * 0.2, gH);
                    }
                    const nextW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[pR]?.[(pC+1)%cols] || false) : !(structure[pR]?.[(pC+1)%cols] || false);
                    if (nextW) {
                        ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${depth})`;
                        ctx.fillRect(gX + gW * 0.8, gY, gW * 0.2, gH);
                    }
                }
            } else {
                // If weft is "Under", check if it's an Extra Weft that should be visible as a float
                const yid = weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length];
                const def = weftYarns[yid];
                if (def?.isExtraWeft && !hideFloats) {
                    const op = def.extraFloatOpacity ?? 0.12;
                    ctx.globalAlpha = op;
                    ctx.drawImage(weftCanvas, warpPositions[c].x, gY, warpPositions[c].w, gH, warpPositions[c].x, gY, warpPositions[c].w, gH);
                    ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // Pass 3: Final Surface Warps (Where warp is "Over")
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        const gY = rowY[r], gH = rowHeights[r];

        for (let c = 0; c < totalCols; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const wTopR = structure[pR]?.[pC] || false;
            const warpIsOver = viewSide === 'face' ? wTopR : !wTopR;

            if (warpIsOver) {
                const gX = warpPositions[c].x, gW = warpPositions[c].w;
                // Clip from continuous warp buffer
                ctx.drawImage(warpCanvas, gX - 0.5, gY, gW + 1.0, gH, gX - 0.5, gY, gW + 1.0, gH);

                // Vertical physical shadow
                const waYid = warpYarnSequence[pC % warpYarnSequence.length];
                const waDef = warpYarns[waYid];
                const depth = (waDef?.bindingDepth || 0.1) * 0.8;
                if (depth > 0) {
                    const upW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[(pR-1+rows)%rows]?.[pC] || false) : !(structure[(pR-1+rows)%rows]?.[pC] || false);
                    if (!upW) { // Weft was over above
                        ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${depth})`;
                        ctx.fillRect(gX, gY, gW, gH * 0.2);
                    }
                    const dnW = viewSide === 'face' ? (structure[(pR+1)%rows]?.[pC] || false) : !(structure[(pR+1)%rows]?.[pC] || false);
                    if (!dnW) { // Weft is over below
                        ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${depth})`;
                        ctx.fillRect(gX, gY + gH * 0.8, gW, gH * 0.2);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return canvas;
};

import { YarnDefinition } from '../types';

const hexToRgb = (hex: string) => {
    hex = hex.replace(/^#/, '');
    return {
        r: parseInt(hex.substring(0, 2), 16),
        g: parseInt(hex.substring(2, 4), 16),
        b: parseInt(hex.substring(4, 6), 16)
    };
};

const lerp = (a: number, b: number, t: number) => a + (b - a) * t;

const generateSeamlessNoise1D = (length: number, scale: number = 1.0): Float32Array => {
    const buffer = new Float32Array(length);
    const period = Math.max(1, Math.floor(length / scale));
    const rawNoise = new Float32Array(period);
    for(let i=0; i<period; i++) rawNoise[i] = Math.random();

    for(let i=0; i<length; i++) {
        const x = (i / length) * period;
        const i0 = Math.floor(x);
        const i1 = (i0 + 1) % period; 
        const t = x - i0;
        const smoothT = t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
        buffer[i] = rawNoise[i0] * (1 - smoothT) + rawNoise[i1] * smoothT;
    }
    return buffer;
};

const CACHE_SIZE_LIMIT = 200;
const textureCache = new Map<string, HTMLCanvasElement>();

const generateYarnHash = (yarn: YarnDefinition, dpi: number): string => {
    return `${yarn.color}-${yarn.colorB}-${yarn.colorC}-${yarn.model}-${yarn.construction}-${yarn.thickness}-${yarn.twist}-${yarn.tpi}-${yarn.sheen}-${yarn.roughness}-${yarn.shadowStrength}-${yarn.hairiness}-${yarn.hairLength}-${yarn.hairCurl}-${yarn.hairThickness}-${yarn.unevenness}-${yarn.slubMode}-${yarn.slubLength}-${yarn.slubDistance}-${yarn.slubAmplitude}-${yarn.spaceDyeLength}-${yarn.pileLength}-${yarn.coreColor}-${dpi}`;
};

export const generateYarnTexture = (yarn: YarnDefinition, dpi: number = 144): HTMLCanvasElement => {
    const hash = generateYarnHash(yarn, dpi);
    if (textureCache.has(hash)) return textureCache.get(hash)!;

    const { 
        color, colorB, colorC, model, construction, twist, tpi, 
        sheen, roughness, shadowStrength = 0.8,
        hairiness = 0, hairLength = 0.2, hairCurl = 0, hairThickness = 1.0,
        unevenness = 0, spaceDyeLength = 10,
        slubMode = 'periodic', slubLength = 0, slubDistance = 0, slubAmplitude = 0, slubColor,
        pileLength = 1.0, fiberType
    } = yarn;

    const pxPerMm = dpi / 25.4;
    const isChenille = construction === 'chenille';
    const isSlubActive = ((slubLength > 0.1 || (yarn.slubLength || 0) > 0) && (slubAmplitude > 10 || (yarn.slubAmplitude || 0) > 0));

    let width = 2048;
    const coreHeight = Math.min(64, Math.max(16, Math.floor(dpi / 4))); 
    const pLenPx = (pileLength || 0.1) * pxPerMm;

    // Physical Headroom Fix: Increased to 5x coreHeight to accommodate ultra-slubs without clipping
    const height = Math.max(1, Math.floor(isChenille ? (coreHeight + pLenPx * 3) : (coreHeight * 5)));
    const centerY = height / 2;

    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = width;
    canvas.height = height;

    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: true });
    if (!ctx) return canvas;

    const colA = hexToRgb(color);
    const colB = colorB ? hexToRgb(colorB) : colA;
    const colSlub = slubColor ? hexToRgb(slubColor) : colA;

    const L = { x: -0.2, y: -0.3, z: 1.0 };
    const lenL = Math.sqrt(L.x*L.x + L.y*L.y + L.z*L.z);
    L.x/=lenL; L.y/=lenL; L.z/=lenL;

    const imgData = ctx.createImageData(width, height);
    const data = imgData.data;

    const slubProfile = new Float32Array(width).fill(1.0);
    if (isSlubActive) {
        const sLen = (slubLength || 2) * pxPerMm;
        const sDist = (slubDistance || 10) * pxPerMm;
        const amp = (slubAmplitude || 50) / 100;
        const cycle = sLen + sDist;
        for(let x=0; x<width; x++) {
            const phase = (x % cycle) / cycle;
            if (phase < (sLen/cycle)) slubProfile[x] = 1.0 + amp;
        }
    }

    const fiberNoise = generateSeamlessNoise1D(width, 2.0); 

    for (let x = 0; x < width; x++) {
        const thicknessMod = slubProfile[x] * (1.0 + (fiberNoise[x]-0.5) * unevenness * 0.4);
        const currentRadius = (coreHeight / 2) * thicknessMod;
        const minY = Math.floor(centerY - currentRadius);
        const maxY = Math.ceil(centerY + currentRadius);

        for (let y = minY; y <= maxY; y++) {
            if (y < 0 || y >= height) continue;
            const ny = (y - centerY) / currentRadius;
            const idx = (y * width + x) * 4;
            const cylinderDepth = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, 1.0 - ny*ny));

            const diffuse = Math.max(0, (ny*L.y + cylinderDepth*L.z) * 0.7 + 0.3);
            const specular = Math.pow(Math.max(0, ny*L.y + cylinderDepth*L.z), 10 + sheen * 50) * sheen;

            const r = lerp(colA.r, colB.r, fiberNoise[(x+y)%width]);
            const g = lerp(colA.g, colB.g, fiberNoise[(x+y)%width]);
            const b = lerp(colA.b, colB.b, fiberNoise[(x+y)%width]);

            data[idx] = Math.min(255, r * diffuse + specular * 255);
            data[idx+1] = Math.min(255, g * diffuse + specular * 255);
            data[idx+2] = Math.min(255, b * diffuse + specular * 255);
            data[idx+3] = 255;
        }
    }
    ctx.putImageData(imgData, 0, 0);

    // Hairiness pass
    if (hairiness > 0) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${colA.r}, ${colA.g}, ${colA.b}, 0.4)`;
        ctx.lineWidth = hairThickness;
        for(let i=0; i<hairiness * 2000; i++) {
            const x = Math.random() * width;
            const y = centerY + (Math.random()-0.5) * coreHeight;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(x, y);
            ctx.lineTo(x + (Math.random()-0.5) * 10, y + (Math.random()-0.5) * 10);
            ctx.stroke();
        }
    }

    textureCache.set(hash, canvas);
    return canvas;
};

import { YarnDefinition, DensityZone } from '../types';
import { generateYarnTexture } from './yarnRenderer';

interface RenderOptions {
    weavePattern: string[][];
    structure: boolean[][];
    epi: number;
    ppi: number;
    dentingPlan?: number[];
    weftZones?: DensityZone[];
    warpYarns: { [key: string]: YarnDefinition };
    weftYarns: { [key: string]: YarnDefinition };
    warpYarnSequence: string[];
    weftYarnSequence: string[];
    viewSide: 'face' | 'back';
    dpi: number;
    width: number; 
    height: number; 
    hideFloats?: boolean; 
    backgroundColor?: string; 
    smoothingQuality?: 'low' | 'medium' | 'high' | 'none';
}

/**
 * FABRIC RENDERER V16.0 - PHYSICAL INTERLACEMENT ENGINE (PIE)
 * Optimized for high-cover density and zero-gap rendering.
 */
export const renderFabricToCanvas = (options: RenderOptions): HTMLCanvasElement => {
    const { 
        weavePattern = [], structure = [], epi, ppi, dentingPlan,
        warpYarns = {}, weftYarns = {}, warpYarnSequence = [], weftYarnSequence = [],
        viewSide, dpi, width: displayW, height: displayH,
        hideFloats = false,
        backgroundColor: requestedBg = '#050505',
        smoothingQuality = 'high'
    } = options;

    const rows = weavePattern.length;
    const cols = weavePattern[0] ? weavePattern[0].length : 0;
    if (rows === 0 || cols === 0) return document.createElement('canvas');

    // --- STABLE GRID CALCULATION ---
    const SS_FACTOR = 1.25; 
    const PX_PER_INCH = dpi * SS_FACTOR;
    const CANVAS_WIDTH = Math.round((displayW / 96) * PX_PER_INCH);
    const CANVAS_HEIGHT = Math.round((displayH / 96) * PX_PER_INCH);

    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = Math.max(1, CANVAS_WIDTH);
    canvas.height = Math.max(1, CANVAS_HEIGHT);
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false });
    if (!ctx) return canvas;

    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = smoothingQuality !== 'none';

    // --- STEP 0: SUBSTRATE PRE-FILL ---
    // Derived from the palette to eliminate high-contrast black bleed
    const avgWarpHex = warpYarns[warpYarnSequence[0]]?.color || '#111';
    ctx.fillStyle = requestedBg === '#ffffff' ? '#ffffff' : '#08080a';
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

    // --- GEOMETRY SETUP ---
    const NOMINAL_W = PX_PER_INCH / Math.max(1, epi);
    const NOMINAL_H = PX_PER_INCH / Math.max(1, ppi);

    const warpPositions: {x: number, w: number}[] = [];
    let currentX = 0;
    for(let i=0; i < cols * 2; i++) { // Double for tiling
        warpPositions.push({ x: currentX, w: NOMINAL_W });
        currentX += NOMINAL_W;
        if (currentX > CANVAS_WIDTH + 100) break;
    }

    const rowY: {y: number, h: number}[] = [];
    let currentY = 0;
    for(let i=0; i < rows * 2; i++) {
        rowY.push({ y: currentY, h: NOMINAL_H });
        currentY += NOMINAL_H;
        if (currentY > CANVAS_HEIGHT + 100) break;
    }

    // --- TEXTURE MAP ---
    const textures = new Map<string, HTMLCanvasElement>();
    const getTex = (id: string, type: 'warp' | 'weft') => {
        const key = `${type}-${id}`;
        if (textures.has(key)) return textures.get(key);
        const def = (type === 'warp' ? warpYarns : weftYarns)[id];
        if (!def) return null;
        const t = generateYarnTexture(def, PX_PER_INCH / 4);
        textures.set(key, t);
        return t;
    };

    /**
     * MICRO-CELL COMPOSITOR
     */
    const drawSegment = (tex: HTMLCanvasElement, gx: number, gy: number, gw: number, gh: number, isV: boolean, thickness: number, opacity: number = 1.0, ao: number = 0) => {
        if (!tex || opacity <= 0) return;

        // Physical Cover Expansion (1.2x) kills lateral gaps
        const lateralExpansion = 1.25;
        // Sub-pixel Extension (0.8px) kills longitudinal gaps
        const longitudinalExtension = 0.8;

        let dw, dh, dx, dy;
        if (isV) {
            dw = gw * thickness * lateralExpansion;
            dh = gh + longitudinalExtension * 2;
            dx = gx + gw/2 - dw/2;
            dy = gy - longitudinalExtension;
        } else {
            dh = gh * thickness * lateralExpansion;
            dw = gw + longitudinalExtension * 2;
            dy = gy + gh/2 - dh/2;
            dx = gx - longitudinalExtension;
        }

        ctx.save();
        ctx.globalAlpha = opacity;
        const phase = Math.floor((Math.abs(Math.sin((isV ? gx : gy) * 44.12)) * 5000) % tex.width);

        if (isV) {
            ctx.translate(dx + dw/2, dy + dh/2);
            ctx.rotate(Math.PI / 2);
            ctx.drawImage(tex, (gy + phase) % tex.width, 0, 1, tex.height, -dh/2, -dw/2, dh, dw);
        } else {
            ctx.drawImage(tex, (gx + phase) % tex.width, 0, 1, tex.height, dx, dy, dw, dh);
        }

        if (ao > 0) {
            ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0,0,0,${ao})`;
            if (isV) ctx.fillRect(-dh/2, -dw/2, dh, dw);
            else ctx.fillRect(dx, dy, dw, dh);
        }
        ctx.restore();
    };

    // PASS 1: GROUND THREADS (The "Under" layer)
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        for (let c = 0; c < warpPositions.length; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const warpIsUp = structure[pR]?.[pC] ?? false;
            const weftIsOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !warpIsUp : warpIsUp;

            if (weftIsOver) {
                // Warp is UNDER
                const yid = warpYarnSequence[pC % warpYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
                const def = warpYarns[yid];
                if (def) drawSegment(getTex(yid, 'warp')!, warpPositions[c].x, rowY[r].y, warpPositions[c].w, rowY[r].h, true, def.thickness || 1);
            } else {
                // Weft is UNDER
                const yid = weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
                const def = weftYarns[yid];
                if (def) {
                    const op = def.isExtraWeft ? (hideFloats ? 0 : (def.extraFloatOpacity ?? 0.1)) : 1.0;
                    drawSegment(getTex(yid, 'weft')!, warpPositions[c].x, rowY[r].y, warpPositions[c].w, rowY[r].h, false, def.thickness || 1, op);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // PASS 2: BINDING SHADOWS
    // We only apply this where a thread is about to go "under"
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        for (let c = 0; c < warpPositions.length; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const warpIsUp = structure[pR]?.[pC] ?? false;
            const weftIsOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !warpIsUp : warpIsUp;

            if (weftIsOver) {
                // Check if weft needs shadow (coming from an 'under' state)
                const prevWarpUp = structure[pR]?.[(pC-1+cols)%cols] ?? false;
                const prevWeftOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !prevWarpUp : prevWarpUp;
                if (!prevWeftOver) {
                    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.3)';
                    ctx.fillRect(warpPositions[c].x, rowY[r].y, warpPositions[c].w * 0.3, rowY[r].h);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // PASS 3: SURFACE THREADS (The "Over" layer)
    for (let r = 0; r < rowY.length; r++) {
        const pR = r % rows;
        for (let c = 0; c < warpPositions.length; c++) {
            const pC = c % cols;
            const warpIsUp = structure[pR]?.[pC] ?? false;
            const warpIsOver = viewSide === 'face' ? warpIsUp : !warpIsUp;

            if (warpIsOver) {
                const yid = warpYarnSequence[pC % warpYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
                const def = warpYarns[yid];
                if (def) drawSegment(getTex(yid, 'warp')!, warpPositions[c].x, rowY[r].y, warpPositions[c].w, rowY[r].h, true, def.thickness || 1);
            } else {
                const yid = weftYarnSequence[pR % weftYarnSequence.length] || 'A';
                const def = weftYarns[yid];
                const isActuallyOver = viewSide === 'face' ? !warpIsUp : warpIsUp;
                if (def && isActuallyOver) {
                    drawSegment(getTex(yid, 'weft')!, warpPositions[c].x, rowY[r].y, warpPositions[c].w, rowY[r].h, false, def.thickness || 1);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return canvas;
};
